    "about": "A three-dimensional cousin of the sine-and-cosine attractors, named after Clifford Pickover. A point drifts through 3D space following coupled trigonometric rules, weaving a ribbon- or shell-like cloud you can view from any angle. All starting points converge to the same 3D attractor.",
