    "about": "A reaction-diffusion field where two virtual chemicals, U and V, spread out and react on a wrap-around grid. U is steadily fed in while V is removed; where they mix, V multiplies and eats U, producing spots, stripes, mazes, and dividing-cell patterns. It is the Gray-Scott model, famous for looking uncannily like living tissue or coral growing on its own.",
